96
00:12:06,546 --> 00:12:07,671
Tool of the Week.

97
00:12:07,671 --> 00:12:15,108
Liquid AI LFM2.5-24B-A2B – Reasoning MoE for On-Device Agents.

98
00:12:15,108 --> 00:12:26,221
The model has 24B parameters, 2B of them active per token, and according to the vendor targets fast, private agents with strengths in tool use and instruction following .

99
00:12:26,221 --> 00:12:37,621
Per the vendor, it reaches 184 tokens/s on an Apple M5 Max and 114 tokens/s on a Ryzen AI Max+ 395 .

100
00:12:37,621 --> 00:12:47,571
Runtimes are llama.cpp, MLX, vLLM, SGLang and ONNX, and the context is 131K tokens .

101
00:12:47,571 --> 00:13:18,121
Compared with Qwen3.6-35B-A3B, it leads on AutomationBench (27.69 vs. 8.72) and IFEval (96.75 vs. 93.06) and trails on GPQA Diamond (74.42 vs. 83.69) and SWE-Bench Verified (51.00 vs. 66.20) (vendor figures, not independently verified) .

102
00:13:18,121 --> 00:13:23,396
For knowledge and coding, Liquid AI recommends adding retrieval or web search .

103
00:13:23,396 --> 00:13:31,633
Unlike Muse Spark Open, it is designed for on-device use; whether it runs smoothly on a specific laptop depends on the hardware .

104
00:13:31,633 --> 00:13:35,421
The license appears only on the model card and we did not check it.

105
00:13:35,421 --> 00:13:36,483
View the model

106
00:13:36,483 --> 00:13:37,633
Fail of the Week.

107
00:13:37,633 --> 00:13:43,708
"Meta's business terms may have allowed AI training on website content – Meta removes the wording"

108
00:13:43,708 --> 00:13:55,646
Meta's new business terms (effective October 30) reportedly contained a clause that could allow Meta to use website content for AI training; Verge coverage puts news sites and publishers at the center  .

109
00:13:55,646 --> 00:13:59,608
Legal experts criticized the wording as strikingly far-reaching .

110
00:13:59,608 --> 00:14:08,446
After the criticism, Meta removed the wording; a Meta spokesperson said, roughly, that this does not change how Meta uses web crawlers .

111
00:14:08,446 --> 00:14:14,308
According to Meta, the consolidated crawling terms related only to ads and business products .

112
00:14:14,308 --> 00:14:17,896
We had only the title and short description of the Verge source .

113
00:14:17,896 --> 00:14:21,271
The publishers' perspective is not covered in our material.

114
00:14:21,271 --> 00:14:30,046
For website operators in the EU, there is also the question of copyright and text-and-data-mining reservations, which the reports do not address.

115
00:14:30,146 --> 00:14:40,421
Root Cause: Multiple purposes (ads crawling and AI training) were apparently bundled into one consolidated clause whose reach was not apparent to outsiders.

116
00:14:40,421 --> 00:14:44,696
This is an interpretation based on the reports, not a statement from Meta.

117
00:14:44,696 --> 00:14:49,608
Whether intent or imprecise drafting was behind it is not established.

118
00:14:49,608 --> 00:14:59,871
What we learn: Anyone changing terms and conditions should name the purpose of data use separately and unambiguously; otherwise the public decides how the clause is read.

119
00:14:59,871 --> 00:15:01,008
